---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/HeroSection.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import SignsList from '../components/SignsList.astro';

const signs = [
  'Doors or windows that have recently started sticking',
  'New cracks appearing in interior drywall',
  'Tile or hardwood floors that have cracked or buckled',
  'Visible gaps between your exterior trim and the wall',
  'Uneven floors in a home that previously felt level',
];
---

<Layout
  title="Foundation Repair in Bullard, TX | Tyler Foundation Pros"
  description="Foundation settling or cracking in Bullard, TX? Tyler Foundation Pros serves Bullard with expert slab repair and house leveling. Free inspection. Call (903) 555-1234."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <HeroSection
    h1="Expert Foundation Repair in Bullard, TX"
    subheading="Tyler Foundation Pros serves Bullard homeowners with free inspections and permanent foundation repair solutions, including steel pier systems and house leveling."
    buttonText="Call (903) 555-1234 — Free Bullard Inspection"
  />

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg mb-4">
        Bullard, TX is known for its larger lots, newer custom builds, and proximity to Lake Palestine. It's one of the more upscale communities in the Tyler area — which also means higher-value homes where foundation problems carry significant financial risk.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg">
        Tyler Foundation Pros serves Bullard homeowners with free inspections and permanent foundation repair solutions, including steel pier systems and house leveling.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why New Construction Still Settles -->
  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Why New Construction in Bullard Still Settles</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Many Bullard homes are newer construction — built within the last 10 to 20 years. Homeowners sometimes assume newer homes don't have foundation problems, but the reality is that new construction on disturbed soil can actually settle faster than older homes.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        When land is cleared and graded for development, the disturbed soil takes years to fully compact. Combined with East Texas clay, this creates predictable settlement patterns in the first decade after construction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Cost Reality -->
  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">What Bullard Foundation Repairs Cost</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        Because Bullard homes tend to be larger and higher-value, foundation repairs often involve more pier points and more square footage than a typical Tyler home. Repairs in the Bullard area frequently range from $8,000 to $20,000+ for complex jobs — making it critical to address problems before they compound.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Signs -->
  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Signs Your Bullard Home Needs Foundation Work</h2>
      <SignsList items={signs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <CTASection
    heading="Schedule Your Free Bullard Inspection"
    subtext="High-value home. Honest assessment. Local experts. We'll inspect your foundation and give you a straight answer about what's going on."
    buttonText="Call (903) 555-1234 — Free Bullard Inspection"
  />
</Layout>
